# The framework. Not tracked: either a relative symlink to the workspace's live psxport checkout
# (local) or a clone of its main (fresh machine). Managed by tools/psxport_fetch.py.
/external/psxport

# Ad-hoc attached-debugger scripts. A gdb script needs a live process with a debugger attached and its
# breakpoints change what it measures — this one says so itself, noting that an unconditional
# breakpoint on another title altered the run's outcome because the host field clock is wall-clock
# driven. That makes it a scratch instrument, not repository surface: nothing can gate on it, and
# tracking it would imply a reproducibility it does not have. The durable answer to the same question
# is a scripted measurement over the product's own control channel, which is what
# tools/probe_loader_state.py is.
tools/probe_*.gdb
